\ The Registers view's reads and writes, as a debugger makes them (dpeek,  ok.
\ dpoke): reads without side effects, writes with them  ok.
#!dpeek 48000000 4002104C E000E010
48000000: EBFFFFAF
4002104C: 0000002F
E000E010: 00000000
\ PA5 an output, driven high, by poking MODER and BSRR  ok.
#!dpoke 48000000 EBFFF7AF
#!dpoke 48000018 00000020
$48000000 @ hex. EBFFF7AF  ok.
$48000014 @ hex. 00000020  ok.
#!dpeek 48000014
48000014: 00000020
\ A poke into SysTick (the core's System Control Space) and into RAM  ok.
#!dpoke E000E014 00001234
$E000E014 @ hex. 00001234  ok.
#!dpoke 20007000 CAFEF00D
$20007000 @ hex. CAFEF00D  ok.
\ A peripheral with its clock off: the write is lost, as on the chip  ok.
#!dpoke 40013808 00001234

[chip] USART1 written while its clock is off in RCC: the write is lost (PC 0x00002514)
#!dpeek 40013808
40013808: 00000000
\ Nothing there: a bus error  ok.
#!dpoke 60000000 1
dpoke: bus error

[chip] Bus error: write to 0x60000000, where there is no memory or peripheral (PC 0x00002514)
